{"kind":"propose","text":"Decision: the kernel remains semantic-free. The application submit path owns parsing canonical event identifiers, determining whether a reference names this workroom, and refusing an in-log reference that does not resolve. The kernel must perform every representation-level identifier validation it can perform without learning application semantics, including the existing non-empty, bounds, count, and control-byte checks and any further format-independent validity check that can be proved useful. If a validity check requires recognizing genesis-plus-commit syntax or resolving an event, it belongs in the application rather than the kernel.","body":{"decision":"application-resolves-kernel-validates-opaque-form"}}